# Sources for the Front's public and oil campaign: Fakhreddin Azimi,
# Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953, ch. 5, pp. 250–267;
# Painter and Brew, The Struggle for Iran, ch. 1.
# The recurring meeting and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Public Meetings
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: public_campaign
view-if: public_meetings_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; public_meetings_timer = 3

= Public Meetings

Public meetings can display a common mandate, recruit new organizers, and
generate reports from beyond the leadership circle. The same people and money
cannot produce both one highly visible gathering and a broad circuit of local
meetings.

Decide whether this month calls for concentration or reach.

- @meetings_tehran
- @meetings_network

@meetings_tehran
title: Concentrate scarce organizers in Tehran
subtitle: One great gathering draws on the common purse, makes the <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span> impossible to overlook, and gives the <span class="term term-royalist">Crown</span> a single target
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; public_mandate += 6; press_capacity += 2; shah_resistance += 2

The secretariat brings its best speakers, marshals, and press contacts into one
Tehran gathering. The visible crowd gives friendly papers a clear image of
public support and gives participants the sense of acting together.

The demonstration is difficult for the
{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court{!</span>!} to ignore. It strengthens the
mandate while making royal resistance more likely.

- @post_event: Continue

@meetings_network
title: Coordinate several smaller meetings
subtitle: Several modest halls train local organizers without creating one dramatic confrontation
on-arrival: organizational_reach += 4; independent_nationalists_organization += 2; toilers_organization += 2

Instead of one central event, organizers share speaking notes and reporting
forms across several smaller meetings. {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Independent nationalists{!</span>!} and
{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!}
gain practical experience arranging rooms, speakers, and follow-up contacts.

No single gathering dominates the news. The coalition finishes the month with
more people able to organize the next one.

- @post_event: Continue
